ction_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [485, 675, 956, 1253], \"page_id\": 6}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [57, 910, 356, 1200], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [153, 248, 1304, 536], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"TREASURY BULLETIN\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [576, 1032, 1036, 1087], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"DECEMBER - 1954\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 1667, 1299, 1723], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"UNITED STATES TREASURY DEPARTMENT\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 1736, 1299, 1771], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"OFFICE OF THE SECRETARY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [7, 40, 214, 82], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"December 1954\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [516, 219, 894, 270], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Table of Contents\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1105, 352, 1194, 388], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Fage\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [214, 407, 1203, 1442], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Treasury financing operations</td><td>A-1</td></tr><tr><td>Summary of Federal fiscal operations</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Budget receipts and expenditures</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Trust account and other transactions</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury cash income and outgo</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Debt outstanding and Treasurer's account</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Statutory debt limitation</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Debt operations</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td>United States savings bonds</td><td>21</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury savings notes</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>Ownership of Federal securities</td><td>26</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury survey of ownership of Federal securities</td><td>28</td></tr><tr><td>Market quotations on Treasury securities</td><td>32</td></tr><tr><td>Average yields of long-term bonds</td><td>35</td></tr><tr><td>Internal revenue collections</td><td>37</td></tr><tr><td>Monetary statistics</td><td>41</td></tr><tr><td>Capital movements</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>Cumulative table of contents</td><td>57</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [224, 1484, 1198, 1583], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Note: Where calculations have been made from unrounded figures, the details may not check to the totals shown.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [305, 840, 1155, 971], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"The Treasury Bulletin is for sale by the Superintendent of Documents, U. S. Government Printing Office, Washington 25, D. C. Subscription per year $4.25 domestic, $5.25 foreign. Single copy price varies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [23, 9, 240, 40], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"December 1954\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1385, 9, 1436, 42], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"A-1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [494, 100, 961, 140], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Treasury Financing Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [57, 168, 527, 199], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"$17.3 Billion Bond and Note Refunding\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [55, 204, 676, 642], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"On November 18, 1954, the Treasury Department announced that in exchange for its three December bond and note maturities (including the 2 percent bonds of 1951-55 called for redemption on December 15, 1954) it would offer on November 22 three securities: 8-year and 8-month 2-1/2 percent Treasury bonds, one-year 1-1/4 percent certificates of indebtedness, and an additional amount of 1-1/8 percent certificates of indebtedness, Series D-1955, which will mature in August 1955. Holders of the maturing issues were given the option of subscribing for any or all of the securities offered and exchanges were made par for par. The subscription books were closed at the close of business on November 24.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [54, 664, 684, 799], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Exchanges amounted to $17.0 billion, more than 98 percent of the total, leaving $316 million to be paid in cash. The results of the refinancing are summarized in the following table.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [738, 157, 1359, 392], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"The 1-1/4 percent certificates, Series E-1955, are dated December 15, 1954, and bear interest at the rate of 1-1/4 percent per annum, payable at their maturity on December 15, 1955. They were issued in bearer form only, in the same denominations as the new bonds except that the denomination of $500 was not made available.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [738, 416, 1366, 802], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"The additional amount of the 1-1/8 percent certificates, Series D-1955, are part of the series first issued in August 1954 (with which they are freely interchangeable) and are identical except for authorization of their issuance in the two additional denominations of $100,000,000 and $500,000,000. These certificates are dated August 15, 1954, and bear interest at the rate of 1-1/8 percent per annum, payable at their maturity on August 15, 1955. For exchange into this issue, the full six months' interest due on December 15, 1954, on the securities surrendered was credited,\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [96, 813, 1302, 1428], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Maturing securities</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Outstanding September 30, 1954</th><th colspan=\\\"4\\\">Securities issued in exchange</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Payable in cash</th><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Maturing securities held by the bank system September 30, 1954 1/ (Percent)</th></tr><tr><th>Total</th><th>1-1/8 percent certificates, Series D-1955</th><th>1-1/4 percent certificates, Series E-1955</th><th>2-1/2 percent bonds of 1963</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"2\\\">(In millions)</td><td colspan=\\\"4\\\"></td><td></td><td>(Percent)</td></tr><tr><td>1-7/8 percent notes, Series B-1954, maturing December 15, 1954....</td><td>$8,175</td><td>$8,133</td><td>$4,498</td><td>$3,289</td><td>$346</td><td>$42</td><td>89</td></tr><tr><td>2 percent bonds of 1952-54, dated December 1, 1944, maturing December 15, 1954.</td><td>8,662</td><td>8,422</td><td>407</td><td>1,985</td><td>6,030</td><td>240</td><td>66</td></tr><tr><td>2 percent bonds of 1951-55, dated December 15, 1941, called for redemption on December 15, 1954..</td><td>510</td><td>476</td><td>14</td><td>87</td><td>375</td><td>34</td><td>65</td></tr><tr><td>Total</td><td>17,347</td><td>17,031</td><td>4,920</td><td>5,360</td><td>6,751</td><td>316</td><td>77</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [103, 1428, 1274, 1506], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"1/ Owned by reporting commercial banks and Federal Reserve Banks. The ownership figures for September 30 are the latest published for holdings of commercial banks reporting to the Treasury on the ownership of Government securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [47, 1537, 677, 1827], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"The new bonds are dated December 15, 1954, and bear interest from that date at the rate of 2-1/2 percent per annum, payable on a semiannual basis on August 15, 1955, and thereafter on February 15 and August 15 in each year until the principal amount becomes payable at maturity on August 15, 1963. They were issued in registered and coupon form, in denominations of $500, $1,000, $5,000, $10,000, $100,000, $1,000,000, $100,000,000, and $500,000,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [731, 1534, 1361, 1643], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"accrued interest from August 15 to December 15 on the new certificates was charged, and the subscribers were paid the difference.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [731, 1665, 999, 1698], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Call before Maturity\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [738, 1703, 1362, 1833], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"On November 15, 1954, the Treasury Department issued notice that the 2-7/8 percent Treasury bonds of 1955-60, dated March 15, 1935, due March 15, 1960, are called for redemption on March 15, 1955, when\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [41, 33, 81, 53], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"A-2\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1204, 20, 1438, 58], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [92, 175, 699, 229], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"interest on these bonds will cease. There are $2.611 million of the issue outstanding.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [91, 280, 699, 473], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"The announcement stated that holders may, in advance of the redemption date, be offered the privilege of exchanging all or any part of their called bonds for other interest-bearing obligations of the United States, in which event public notice will be given.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [776, 169, 1061, 191], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bills Refunded\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [776, 200, 1384, 473], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"November maturities of Treasury bills amounting to $6.0 billion were refunded in full by four weekly issues of approximately $1.5 billion each. New 91-day bills, dated November 4 and 18, refunded like maturities and new 90-day bills, dated November 12 and 26, refunded maturing 92-day bills. The average rates of discount on the new issues were 1.023 percent for November 4; 0.940 percent for November 12; 0.931 percent for November 18; and 0.897 percent for November 26.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [122, 526, 170, 544], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"Note:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 520, 722, 586], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"Details of Treasury market financing operations are shown elsewhere in this issue of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\", in the tables on \\\"Offerings\\\" and \\\"Dis-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [807, 522, 1400, 586], \"page_id\": 12}], \"content\": \"position\\\", respectively, of marketable issues of bonds, notes, and certificates of indebtedness, and in the table \\\"Offerings of Treasury Bills\\\".\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [37, 11, 240, 42], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"December 1954\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}